WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.145
- My knowledge of Hannukah
is the Disney Channel movie

00:00:03.145 --> 00:00:04.367
Full-Court Miracles.

00:00:04.367 --> 00:00:05.976
- What I know vaguely about the story

00:00:05.976 --> 00:00:07.468
I learned from the Rugrats.

00:00:07.468 --> 00:00:11.045
- I know that there's a Menorah.

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:21.594
- You'd have to have letters
that make "kha, kha!"

00:00:21.610 --> 00:00:22.989
- C, H.--

00:00:22.989 --> 00:00:24.834
- H, A.--

00:00:24.834 --> 00:00:26.670
- U, N.--

00:00:26.670 --> 00:00:30.574
- I, K, Haunik, A.

00:00:30.574 --> 00:00:31.786
- K.

00:00:31.786 --> 00:00:33.016
- A.

00:00:37.381 --> 00:00:39.592
- Hannukah celebrates...

00:00:39.592 --> 00:00:41.792
- Was it when they were,

00:00:42.407 --> 00:00:45.390
crossing the Red Sea?

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:47.772
- They only had a little bit of oil.

00:00:47.772 --> 00:00:50.417
- And, through the miracle of the Lord,

00:00:50.417 --> 00:00:53.338
that oil lasted eight nights.

00:00:53.338 --> 00:00:56.357
- That's why everything is fried, I think,

00:00:56.357 --> 00:00:59.502
and why potato pancakes
are the love of my life.

00:01:03.524 --> 00:01:05.808
- Oh my God, I don't even
know how many days it is.

00:01:05.808 --> 00:01:07.601
- It's like seven days, right?

00:01:07.601 --> 00:01:09.603
- I think it's eight days of Hanukkah.

00:01:09.603 --> 00:01:12.272
- There are twelve candles in a Menorah.

00:01:12.272 --> 00:01:14.513
- There are nine candles on the Menorah.

00:01:14.513 --> 00:01:16.633
- 'Cause I think it's one
for every day of the week.

00:01:16.633 --> 00:01:18.312
- Because there's one for every night

00:01:18.312 --> 00:01:20.558
and then there's the one master candle

00:01:20.558 --> 00:01:22.428
that you use to light
all of the other ones.

00:01:25.129 --> 00:01:26.597
- What's a dreidel, I don't know.

00:01:26.597 --> 00:01:27.807
- Don't know what it means.

00:01:27.807 --> 00:01:32.669
- Dreidels are big spoons
that Jewish people use

00:01:32.669 --> 00:01:35.680
to collect matzo balls out of the pot.

00:01:38.537 --> 00:01:41.384
- You spin the dreidel
and then what it falls on,

00:01:41.384 --> 00:01:44.513
you have to do what it says?

00:01:44.513 --> 00:01:47.390
- You get chocolate coins if you win.

00:01:47.390 --> 00:01:51.061
- You win, or you lose,
or you take another turn,

00:01:51.061 --> 00:01:53.681
or you take the other guys coins.

00:01:55.279 --> 00:01:59.445
- I just remember Jewish friends
getting presents all week.

00:01:59.445 --> 00:02:01.522
- Everybody drinks Manischewitz.

00:02:01.522 --> 00:02:03.950
- Maybe they have a Hanukkah
party at the end of it?

00:02:03.950 --> 00:02:06.284
- They sit around in a circle
and they play the guitar.

00:02:06.284 --> 00:02:10.121
- And I think they leave
a seat open for Elijah.

00:02:10.121 --> 00:02:13.101
- And Adam Sandler is
leading the ceremony.

00:02:15.179 --> 00:02:18.504
(upbeat music)

